Telitz, 22, from Birch[wood], Wis., put on another clinic during his[ Semi] Final round. He made an exemplary start from the[ pole] and led all 15 laps to ensure a place on the front row of the grid for the 20-lap Grand Final. He had to be content with the outside position, due to the fact his[ Semi] Final had been interrupted by two[ Safety] Car periods which[ ensured] a slower average speed than[ Semi] Final 2.[ Und]eterred, Telitz made a good start and immediately began to pressurize race leader Jonny McMull[an].
