He said that 140 or so people had participated in the seven tours[ organized] to date.
Iw[aki] resident Kaori Sug[an]ami, 39, took part in a tour last June.
Because of the core meltdowns at the No. 1 to No. 3 reactors, high levels of radiation continue to be emitted. This makes it very difficult to approach those three reactors.
Elsewhere, though, rubble that was stre[wn] throughout the plant grounds due to the tsunami generated by the magnitude-9.[0 Great] East[ Japan] Earthquake has been[ removed], and radiation levels in many areas have dropped significantly.[ Ground] surfaces have been paved and trees felled, which has also helped lower radiation levels.
